# verus/seams.overrides: categories and tools for the seams verus/seams.sh
# cannot classify from the item's kind, path and body, and the status of
# every seam that is no longer only trusted.
#
#   name<TAB>category<TAB>tool[<TAB>status]
#
# `name` is the item as the ledger prints it, `file:name` where several
# items share a name, or `file:name#N` for the Nth of several seams of that
# name in one file (ledger order, which is source order). Category and
# tool are spelled as in the ledger's header; status defaults to
# "trusted" (see "Recording a non-Verus result" in verus/SEAMS.md). A
# line that matches no seam is an error.
